       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 1000 mg once daily is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 200 mg/day. A dose that high risks serotonin syndrome, seizures, and cardiac toxicity (QT prolongation). It looks like a possible typo, such as 100 mg.\n\nYou also mentioned you're in the finance office. Medication orders should come from a licensed prescriber or be verified by one.\n\n- **If this is a typo:** Tell me the intended dose, and ideally confirm it with the prescriber. Typical adult dosing is 25\u2013200 mg once daily. I can enter it once a clinician confirms it.\n- **If the dose is intentional:** The prescriber should enter it directly and document the clinical rationale. Pharmacy will probably need to review it."
